{{header obstacles}}

[[file:Rocks.png|365px]]
* Blocks movement and projectiles unless the player has [[flight]] or [[spectral tears]], respectively.
* Can be destroyed with explosions and certain items like the {{i|Notched Axe}}, {{i|The Nail}}, {{i|Leo}}, or {{i|Thunder Thighs}}.
* Can fill in a 1-block wide gap when pushed in the right direction by an explosion, or with one of the abilities that allows destruction by walking onto the rock.
** Note: With these items, it is important to walk in the direction of the gap.
* Small chance to reveal a {{R|Crawl Space}} when destroyed.
* Destroying 100 rocks will unlock the {{t|Lucky Rock}} trinket.

== Tinted Rocks ==
[[file:Tinted Rocks Repentance.png|422px]]

Sometimes referred to as "Marked Rocks", they are always marked with an "X", and in some levels slightly tinted/discolored. These rocks are much less noticeable in {{s|Womb}}, {{s|Utero}}, and {{s|Scarred Womb}} due to them being the same color as the surrounding rocks, but can still be distinguished by the "X" on the bottom right. Only one tinted rock can spawn per room.
* Destroying 10 Tinted Rocks will unlock {{i|Mr. Mega}}.
* Destroying 100 Tinted Rocks will unlock {{i|The Small Rock}}.
* {{dlc+|r}} Multiple tinted rocks can spawn in one room by using {{p|XVI - The Tower?}}.{{dlc-}}

'''Found in:''' Every Stage

