== Spiked Rocks {{dlc+|r}} ==
[[File:Spiked_Rock.png|50px]]

Spiked Rocks are variants of normal rocks which hurt Isaac on contact, even if he's flying.<br/>
They can fill in a 1-block wide gap like ordinary rocks, but the spikes will remain and Isaac will take damage as he steps on them. If they are located in a room with {{E|Pressure Plate}}s, after all the plates are pressed, the spikes will retract into the interiors of the rock. If a Crawl Space is generated with the same rock used to fill a gap, the bridge will not be spiked.

{{t|Flat File}} will remove the spikes from the rocks.

If spiked rocks are crushed by being {{tf|Stompy}}, having {{i|Leo}} or {{i|Thunder Thighs}}, or using {{i|The Nail}}, they do not always deal damage, depending on Isaac's speed, size, and the angle they are touched from.

'''Found in:''' Every stage except for [[Chapter 6]], {{s|???}} and {{s|Home}}. Additionally, some layouts of {{r|Curse Room}}s, {{r|Super Secret Room}}s, and {{r|Boss Rush}} have spiked rocks.

=== Notes ===
* If a Spiked Rock is used to fill in a gap, stepping on the created spiked path will deal a full heart of damage. This damage is considered self-damage (it will not affect [[Devil Room#Conditions to make Devil Rooms appear|Angel/Devil Deal chances]] and items such as {{i|Paschal Candle}}). Touching Spiked Rocks, however, will not count as self-damage.{{dlc-}}

